=== P18.5: proving final_integrity.sh's FAIL path actually works ===
date: 2026-10-01T01:23:14Z

The first version of the script wrote fail=1 inside a $( ) command substitution -- a
subshell -- so the assignment was discarded and it printed INTEGRITY: PASS while three
checks reported NOT 0. After a fail-open defect, a PASS proves nothing until the FAIL path
is exercised. Three corruptions are applied to a COPY; the real script is never modified.

--- control 0: the unmodified script ---
  exit=0  verdict: INTEGRITY: PASS
--- 1: a must_be_zero check given a non-zero count ---
  exit=1  verdict: INTEGRITY: FAIL
      INJECTED nonzero                             7    *** NOT 0 ***
--- 2: a must_be_nonzero control given 0 (a blind probe) ---
  exit=1  verdict: INTEGRITY: FAIL
      INJECTED blind probe                         0    *** 0 -- THE PROBE IS BLIND ***
--- 3: a wrong expected frozen-gate hash ---
  exit=1  verdict: INTEGRITY: FAIL
      *** THE FROZEN GATE HAS CHANGED ***

EXPECTED: control 0 PASS exit 0; corruptions 1, 2 and 3 each FAIL exit 1.
